WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.029
OK, you are not going to hear me say at any
point during the next six and a half months,

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:08.860
which is the lead up to the November presidential
election.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.860
You

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.260
are not going to hear me say Joe Biden's got
this.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.760
I'm just not going to do it for two reasons.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.280
Number one, I actually believe it's going
to be a fight to the end.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.080
And I think there's a very good chance Donald
Trump ends up getting himself reelected.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.210
But I'm also not going to say it because I
don't want to risk a single person hearing

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.460
me say something like that and deciding that
Joe doesn't need their vote and they can stay

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.410
home or vote third party or whatever the case
may be.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:44.960
There is a path to Trump's reelection that
includes the effects of Corona virus on Democratic

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.530
turnout, combined with Trump successfully
using the virus to bamboozle and goad his

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.210
base into thinking he did a great job with
the virus.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:01:00.270
Plus, Trump doing just enough to keep the
stock market boosted, I think is

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:06.179
the term I would use so that it kind of looks
like the economy is OK even though it's imploding.

00:01:06.179 --> 00:01:09.869
But I also am not going to hide the polling
from you.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.850
So that's why I want to talk today.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.649
We have national polls that look good for
Biden.

00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:18.209
We have state polls that look very, very mixed
for Joe Biden.

00:01:18.209 --> 00:01:22.609
So let's look at some examples, starting with
the general election in the general election.

00:01:22.609 --> 00:01:23.890
Hypothetical polls.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.439
Joe Biden is currently winning by an average
of 5.5 points.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:34.359
Now, this ranges in a tie on Fox News and
Fox News's latest poll all the way up to Biden

00:01:34.359 --> 00:01:37.319
leading by 11 in a recent CNN poll.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:38.359
And everything in between.

00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.700
And the average is that Biden is up 5.5.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.290
Now, let's think about 2016.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:50.149
In 2016, the national polling average going
into the election was Hillary up 3.3.

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:51.149
And

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:54.060
Hillary ended up winning nationally by 2.1.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.279
So the polls were close.

00:01:55.279 --> 00:01:59.149
They were off by about a point in terms of
the national popular vote.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:01.229
Of course, we have an electoral college system.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.409
And despite losing the popular vote badly,
Donald Trump won the Electoral College.

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:11.600
Now, currently, Joe Biden at 5.5 points ahead,
has a much bigger lead than Hillary Clinton

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.600
did.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.660
Going into the 2020 election.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.990
But remember, the Electoral College system
still would allow Donald Trump to win even

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:23.190
if he lost the popular vote by five and a
half points would be a stretch.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:29.270
But if Biden wins the popular vote by four,
it's still very possible that Donald Trump

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.780
could win the Electoral College.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.260
It would be tough, but it would be doable.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.440
So now let's look at some individual states.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.760
North Carolina is not looking great for Joe
Biden.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.770
There's a recent North

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:45.130
Carolina poll where Trump is seven points
ahead of Joe Biden back in 2016.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.240
Trump won North Carolina by only three.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:54.670
If Trump doubles his margin of victory in
North Carolina from 2016 to 2020, it's a signal

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.420
of very bad things for Joe Biden.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.980
But then we've got some places where it's
looking very bad for Donald Trump.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.620
Arizona is one example.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.850
We talked earlier in the show how Republican
incumbent Senator Martha McSally is losing

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.880
by nine to Democratic Senate challenger Mark
Kelly.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.870
Well, Joe Biden is winning by an average of
4.4 and as buttoned by as much as nine in

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.070
one poll in Arizona.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.900
That's a state Trump won in 2016.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:25.070
If Arizona goes from Trump winning by four
to Biden winning by four.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.520
That's an eight point swing.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.680
And it's very, very bad for Donald Trump.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.870
Virginia is another example right now in Virginia.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:33.870
Biden's

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:38.420
winning by an average of seven and by as much
as 10 in the latest poll.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.950
Hillary only won by five in 2016.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:47.470
So, again, if Virginia goes from Hillary plus
five to Biden plus seven, eight or nine or

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.110
even 10, that is very bad for Trump.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.270
So what's the takeaway?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:57.130
The takeaway is, no matter what the polls
say, go and vote.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.380
Ask for an absentee ballot if that's what
your state is doing.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.860
Do not sit this one out because it is likely
to be a huge fight.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:09.770
I was talking over the weekend on Zoom with
a few friends who are very much journalists,

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.959
writers, etc.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:15.230
Many of them feel that November is going to
be a blowout.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.349
They just don't know who's going to win.

00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:20.289
The idea being it won't be close either.

00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:22.629
Biden will very much pull away with it or
Trump will very

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.039
much pull away with it based.

00:04:24.039 --> 00:04:26.680
What's going on with coronavirus in the economy?

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.520
Up if that's the case, then we're going to
have to fight a very, very hard for it to

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.389
be Biden for Biden to be the one who pulls
away.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:37.860
Of course, predictions are often wrong and
it may well be close and it may come down

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.050
to just a couple of states.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.259
So it will be a huge fight.

00:04:41.259 --> 00:04:45.110
Anything that makes you think we've got this
is very dangerous thinking.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.639
And I would encourage you to disabuse yourself
of those notions.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:50.139
Do not get confident.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:52.409
They have every trick up their sleeve.

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:56.990
And with the wild card of coronavirus and
people possibly staying home to avoid the

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.629
virus, anything can happen.

00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:00.629
Anything can happen.

00:05:00.629 --> 00:05:06.909
Last thought, after seeing Donald Trump this
week, talk about how he has absolute power.

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:07.909
He can tell governors what

00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:08.909
to do.

00:05:08.909 --> 00:05:13.550
He can demand and enforce that businesses
be reopened after seeing Trump's authoritarian

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.509
slide this week.

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:20.599
I am increasingly skeptical that Trump would
leave peacefully if he loses to Biden.

00:05:20.599 --> 00:05:22.909
Now, I want to be really careful.

00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:27.300
I'm not saying Trump would succeed in not
leaving.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.559
If Biden wins, I just mean it won't be peaceful.

00:05:30.559 --> 00:05:33.070
In that Trump will claim it was rigged.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.849
He will claim it was stolen.

00:05:34.849 --> 00:05:37.449
He will claim Joe Biden didn't really win.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:39.990
He may even try to start some kind of legal
challenges.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:46.879
I do believe he will leave, but I am increasingly
skeptical that Trump will leave.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:51.510
What I would describe in a peaceful manner,
I do believe he ultimately will leave.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.680
Let me know what you think about that.

